WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.274
Select tools by the workflow problem they solve.

00:00:03.274 --> 00:00:04.861
Search tools discover sources.

00:00:04.861 --> 00:00:07.242
Note applications preserve context and reasoning.

00:00:07.242 --> 00:00:08.829
Spreadsheets support structured comparison.

00:00:08.829 --> 00:00:09.623
Mapping, timeline,

00:00:09.623 --> 00:00:13.987
and link-analysis tools help organize relationships when the requirement justifies them.

00:00:13.987 --> 00:00:16.368
Archive and capture tools support preservation,

00:00:16.368 --> 00:00:20.335
but their output still needs source metadata and handling controls.

00:00:20.335 --> 00:00:23.510
Automation should reduce repetitive work without hiding provenance.

00:00:23.510 --> 00:00:29.858
An analyst must be able to explain where a record came from and what processing changed.

00:00:29.858 --> 00:00:33.429
Local language models may assist with approved summarization, classification,

00:00:33.429 --> 00:00:35.809
or drafting when data handling permits.

00:00:35.809 --> 00:00:39.777
Their output can omit context, invent claims, or blur sources.

00:00:39.777 --> 00:00:42.555
Keep human review, cite the original material,

00:00:42.555 --> 00:00:45.729
and do not treat generated text as evidence.

00:00:45.729 --> 00:00:49.696
Evaluate security, maintenance, export formats, data location, access controls, licensing,

00:00:49.696 --> 00:00:50.490
and support.

00:00:50.490 --> 00:00:55.251
A convenient hosted tool may not be appropriate for sensitive case material.

00:00:55.251 --> 00:01:00.012
A local tool may still be unsafe if unpatched or poorly configured.

00:01:00.012 --> 00:01:01.203
Avoid tool sprawl.

00:01:01.203 --> 00:01:05.567
Too many overlapping utilities increase update burden, inconsistent output, training needs,

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:07.551
and opportunities for data leakage.

00:01:07.551 --> 00:01:10.725
Standardize a small supported set, document its role,

00:01:10.725 --> 00:01:14.693
and retire tools that no longer serve a clear requirement.

00:01:14.693 --> 00:01:19.057
Integrate tools around case identifiers, source logs, file naming, evidence references,

00:01:19.057 --> 00:01:19.851
and reporting.

00:01:19.851 --> 00:01:23.422
Technology should make the workflow safer and more repeatable.

00:01:23.422 --> 00:01:27.390
It should not replace source validation, analytical reasoning, ethical judgment,

00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:28.580
or accountable reporting.
